\n', id='4451bedc-3183-45f9-a03f-9db85149b1f3', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-a3ec9c4d7d0bdb1d'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='07209b35-eaec-4622-b63b-2bf7dcc01daa'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose why the 'recommendation' service is not available. From the previous steps, we saw that the deployment for 'recommendation' has 0/1 replicas available, and the pod is in a Pending state. So the next step is to figure out why the pod can't start.\n\nFirst, I need to check the pod's details. The command 'kubectl describe pod' would give more information about the pending state. Maybe there's an issue with the pod's configuration, like resource limits, node affinity, or image pull problems. Also, checking the events related to the pod could show errors or warnings that indicate the root cause.\n\nThe user has the 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd' tool, so I should use that to run 'kubectl describe pod recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth -n hotel-reservation'. This will provide detailed information about the pod's status, events, and any errors that might be occurring. Looking at the events can help identify if there's a problem with the node, the image, or resource constraints. For example, if the pod is waiting for a node with specific labels, or if the image can't be pulled, that would show up in the describe output. Also, checking the container statuses might reveal if there's a crash loop or if the container isn't starting at all. This information is crucial to determine the next steps in troubleshooting the issue.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The `recommendation` pod is in a `Pending` state, which suggests it hasn't been scheduled to a node. To diagnose this, I need to inspect the pod's details and events. The command `kubectl describe pod recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth -n hotel-reservation` will provide critical information about why the pod is pending, such as resource constraints, node selectors, image pull failures, or scheduling issues. This will help identify the root cause of the deployment failure.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 425, 'prompt_tokens': 4076, 'total_tokens': 4501, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd94-bed6-7d11-a6b1-e27f0e3a2fc0-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4076, 'output_tokens': 425, 'total_tokens': 4501}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='51b42cfe-6e7a-4db2-8b94-987c7b3ec0ca'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the recommendation service is not running. From the previous steps, they checked the deployments and found that the recommendation deployment has 0/1 available replicas. Then they checked the pods and saw that the recommendation pod is in a Pending state. Now, they need to find out why it\'s pending.\n\nThe next logical step is to get more details about that specific pod. Using kubectl describe pod would show events and status reasons. The command should be executed with the pod\'s name, which was given as recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth. The namespace is hotel-reservation. \n\nSo, the tool call should be to exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl describe pod recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth -n hotel-reservation". This will provide information on why the pod isn\'t scheduled, like resource limits, node issues, or image problems. Once they have that info, they can determine the root cause and submit the answer.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bc846e88c1cb9121', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 269, 'prompt_tokens': 5100, 'total_tokens': 5369, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd94-d2e3-7ba3-b415-b40c18389bc8-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bc846e88c1cb9121', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5100, 'output_tokens': 269, 'total_tokens': 5369}), ToolMessage(content="Name:             recommendation-74fd485779-7mjth\nNamespace:        hotel-reservation\nPriority:         0\nService Account:  default\nNode:             <none>\nLabels:           io.kompose.service=recommendation\n                  pod-template-hash=74fd485779\nAnnotations:      kompose.cmd: kompose convert\n                  kompose.version: 1.22.0 (955b78124)\n                  sidecar.istio.io/statsInclusionPrefixes:\n                    cluster.outbound,cluster_manager,listener_manager,http_mixer_filter,tcp_mixer_filter,server,cluster.xds-grp,listener,connection_manager\n                  sidecar.istio.io/statsInclusionRegexps: http.*\nStatus:           Pending\nIP:               \nIPs:              <none>\nControlled By:    ReplicaSet/recommendation-74fd485779\nContainers:\n  hotel-reserv-recommendation:\n    Image:      yinfangchen/hotelreservation:latest\n    Port:       8085/TCP\n    Host Port:  9100/TCP\n    Command:\n      recommendation\n    Limits:\n      cpu:  1\n    Requests:\n      cpu:  100m\n    Environment:\n      JAEGER_SAMPLE_RATIO:  1\n    Mounts:\n      /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount from kube-api-access-lmd68 (ro)\nConditions:\n  Type           Status\n  PodScheduled   False \nVolumes:\n  kube-api-access-lmd68:\n    Type:                    Projected (a volume that contains injected data from multiple sources)\n    TokenExpirationSeconds:  3607\n    ConfigMapName:           kube-root-ca.crt\n    Optional:                false\n    DownwardAPI:             true\nQoS Class:                   Burstable\nNode-Selectors:              <none>\nTolerations:                 node.kubernetes.io/not-ready:NoExecute op=Exists for 300s\n                             node.kubernetes.io/unreachable:NoExecute op=Exists for 300s\nEvents:\n  Type     Reason            Age                From               Message\n  ----     ------            ----               ----               -------\n  Warning  FailedScheduling  48s (x2 over 49s)  default-scheduler  0/3 nodes are available: 3 node(s) didn't have free ports for the requested pod ports. preemption: 0/3 nodes are available: 3 No preemption victims found for incoming pod.\n", id='12d4b4bf-75b3-429c-babd-30c64c1d1ea0', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-bc846e88c1cb9121'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='97bb184d-0834-410e-880f-19d1a38e59aa')]]
