\n\nThe root cause of the failure is a port conflict on all nodes. The `recommendation` pod is configured to use host port `9100`, which is already occupied by another service or process on all available nodes (`node0`, `node1`, `node2`), leading to scheduling failure. This misconfiguration prevents the pod from being assigned to any node.\n\nIn each round, there is a thinking stage. In the thinking stage, you are given a list of tools. Think about what you want to call. Return your tool choice and the reasoning behind.\nWhen choosing the tool, refer to the tool by its name.\nThen, there is a tool-call stage, where you make a tool_call consistent with your explanation.\nYou can run up to 20 rounds to finish the tasks.\nIf you call submit_tool in tool-call stage, the process will end immediately.\nIf you exceed this limitation, the system will force you to make a submission.\nYou will begin by analyzing the service\'s state and telemetry with the tools.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The root cause of the failure is a port conflict on all nodes. The `recommendation` pod is configured to use host port `9100`, which is already occupied by another service or process on all available nodes (`node0`, `node1`, `node2`), leading to scheduling failure. This misconfiguration prevents the pod from being assigned to any node."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=624, prompt_tokens=2085, total_tokens=2709, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd96-72ea-7712-a5fc-39d7b61bf6ab-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2085, 'output_tokens': 624, 'total_tokens': 2709}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_m